{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes","id":1020541,"title":"Do/Will/Should Exigents have Castes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-21T12:11:57-08:00","id":1020541,"title":"Do/Will/Should Exigents have Castes?","content":"The title pretty much says it but if they do/will/should what would they be? Additionally what powers do we think that all extigents should innately have? And lastly what is the title for exigents? (Like Lawgiver or Stewards) I've been using Herald as their title, does that seem appropriate or have other people come up with other titles for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:16:12-08:00","id":1020548,"title":"","content":"Exigents are not a single exalt type, so there are literally <b>zero</b> shared rules. The Exigence allows for the creation of unique exalts from the essence of an existing God. Each creation totally <i>could</i> have castes and rules that associate with it. They could have their own title. But it varies from god to god, so there aren't any unifying rules. <br /> <br /> This is how it is being designed, but if you rule it different in your game that's cool. As far as your second question, I've always loved Herald as a title. In fact, I often look to Bioware games for cool heroic titles (Hero, Champion, Herald, Commander, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:16:40-08:00","id":1020549,"title":"","content":"They won't. Each one is &quot;unique&quot; such that the idea is wholly inappropriate anyway.<br /> <br /> Titles are out, too. Lunars are no longer Stewards, because they felt like contriving titles is unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:21:26-08:00","id":1020553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1020549#post1020549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They won't. Each one is &quot;unique&quot; such that the idea is wholly inappropriate anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Titles are out, too.</b> Lunars are no longer Stewards, because they felt like contriving titles is unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>(emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> This is directly contradicted by the Revana Quin writeup, which tells us that she is an Architect - and pretty clearly implies that there are or at least can be multiple Architects, each basically the same type of Exalt as she but (probably) attached to a different city.<br /> <br /> Some Exigents will be unique. Other Exigents can and will be of a class, to the point of having common mechanics (the writeup alludes to a standard Architect excellency). So it's entirely possible for Exigents to have castes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:22:19-08:00","id":1020555,"title":"","content":"Many Exigents are unique one-offs, in which case Castes/Aspects/etc. wouldn't make a sense at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:29:01-08:00","id":1020560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1020553#post1020553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> This is directly contradicted by the Revana Quin writeup, which tells us that she is an Architect - and pretty clearly implies that there are or at least can be multiple Architects, each basically the same type of Exalt as she but (probably) attached to a different city.<br /> <br /> Some Exigents will be unique. Other Exigents can and will be of a class, to the point of having common mechanics (the writeup alludes to a standard Architect excellency). So it's entirely possible for Exigents to have castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I failed to clarify. Titles are out in the sense that they're not required (like you can have Solars be Lawgivers but Lunars don't have a title anymore, etc.) , not that they're entirely discarded. If we went with the latter, Lawgiver wouldn't make much sense either.<br /> <br /> What I intended to say was that there is absolutely no requirement for a title, so it's good to understand that titles will only really exist in the specific sense or in the archetypal sense. <br /> <br /> I.e. If you include Revana Quin's Charmset as an example of an Exigent in Exigents, you probably will refer to the subject character as an Architect rather than Revana because calling them Revana in the charm text might pull people out of the idea that you could use that Charmset for another character. It's a language thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:34:43-08:00","id":1020562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes#post1020541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title pretty much says it but if they do/will/should what would they be?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends entirely on whether it suits your purposes to have Exigents who are divided by castes. I can definitely see the possibilities for a specific individual god to make a collection of Exigents with slightly different powers. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes#post1020541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Additionally what powers do we think that all extigents should innately have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each one should have powers that reflect the being that empowered them. I cannot think of any specific power that <i>all</i> of them share, regardless of their origin. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes#post1020541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And lastly what is the title for exigents? (Like Lawgiver or Stewards) I've been using Herald as their title, does that seem appropriate or have other people come up with other titles for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Champion works. So does Avatar, Prophet, Luminary, or Blasphemer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:16:33-08:00","id":1020595,"title":"","content":"I like champion, given that the more powerful ones friendly with dragon-blooded probably have a similar role to alchemicals as non-ruling muscle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:58:41-08:00","id":1020627,"title":"","content":"If the god has space for it, and you feel you could in theory think of Caste variations of the Exigent, I think it would be cool.<br /> <br /> To me, like, if you really can think of, for example, a Social / Mental / Physical primary version of the Chosen of that City God you're interested in, there's no reason that you can't put a Caste on it. Perhaps that City God has Castes that mirror eras of his city - Founding Caste, Wartime Caste, Golden Era Caste, Decadence Caste, Ruin Caste. Even if the god only actually ever has one Chosen in your given game. I wouldn't want to close down on people's creativity.<br /> <br /> As a term, Aspect might make more sense than Caste for such variations, since Caste implies a social division in a mass society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 12-21-2016, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T15:27:59-08:00","id":1020679,"title":"","content":"They are of the Special Snowflake caste.<br /> <br /> Sobriquets include: Many-Petaled Ice Flowers, Winter's Tears, and Don't Eat the Yellow Ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T15:52:20-08:00","id":1020686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes#post1020541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And lastly what is the title for exigents? (Like Lawgiver or Stewards)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe title for Janest is Strawmaiden.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Revana Quin writeup, which tells us that she is an Architect</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIs the word Architect equivalent to Lawgiver, or to Solar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T15:57:10-08:00","id":1020687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1020686#post1020686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIs the word Architect equivalent to Lawgiver, or to Solar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Architect is the equivalent of Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T02:07:17-08:00","id":1020804,"title":"","content":"I figured that Architect was shorthand for &quot;And these are the kinds of powers that an Exigent empowered by a city god would use&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like, I doubt that the Exigents book will have Castes, but I figured it might have <i>archetypes</i>. Like &quot;Architects - Urban and City God powered Exigents. Warheroes - For Exigents empowered by Gods of War and Battle&quot;, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T02:27:09-08:00","id":1020809,"title":"","content":"That's my expectation. I expect there will be some example charm trees for different kinds of common Gods' exigents. Animal gods, city gods, war gods, etc. Probably not entire charm sets, but certainly a tree or two. It'd be a lot easier to do that and then also have suggestionss for making your own totally wacky thing... than <i>just</i> having suggestions for making your own entirely wacky thing. Examples are always good... and, more importantly, inspiring!<br /> I was pretty uninterested in Exigents honestly, until I read Ravena Quin's charms, which I found very evocative. Interesting charmsets do inspire you to play stuff, whereas going &quot;make your own!&quot; is pretty uninspiring (to me, at least).<br /> <br /> (Also, if I want to have an NPC Exigent, it'd make it much easier to have some examples, than having to make up an entirely new set of charms for an NPC that might only be there for a session or two)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-22-2016, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T02:41:43-08:00","id":1020810,"title":"","content":"Despite how the developers have said things along the lines of &quot;two different volcano gods will produce entirely different Exalted&quot;?<br /> <br /> I would suppose that Revana Quin has the Architect Excellency because she is an Architect. Even if there is never any other Architect, that's what she is. If one wants to make a different Chosen of a city god with a different term but a similar Excellency, that's probably all fine and dandy, but given absolutely everything that the writers and developers keep trying to tell us about Exigents, it seems very silly to keep wrapping things around to trying to figure out what all Exigents have in common, or even what all Exigents of a particular arbitrary type have in common.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T04:47:27-08:00","id":1020823,"title":"","content":"As I said, examples. Since the whole point is that your Exigent can be anything, I doubt they'd say &quot;all city-god-exigents have these exact charms&quot; because maybe yours is particularly powerful or weak, or there's something unusual about the city (or rather, city-god). But examples are still important and useful.<br /> I'm going to be honest, I'd find it pretty difficult to think up a charm-set for, say, the Exigent of Gem's city-god, with just advice about how to cost charms and build trees. But if there's an example of a bunch of city-god-exigents charms, then I can either use them straight if they fit or modify them if they don't. As I said, the point of having charms in the book isn't just about balance, they're also about inspiration. If the book just says &quot;make your own Exigents! Whatever you want! Here's how to cost their charms,&quot; I'll find it very difficult to make something interesting, tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T08:33:08-08:00","id":1020898,"title":"","content":"I do not think we will get examples for the Chosen of animal gods in general. I think we will get a description of the character of a specific animal god, the circumstances that cause them to pray for the Exigence, and the resulting Exalt.<br /> <br /> \u200bMaybe, for the sake of really driving the point home, there will be two Chosen of different animal gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:12:42-08:00","id":1020915,"title":"","content":"Examples of aspecific one's be fine; as long as there are a bunch of example charms to base other Exigents off (and I do mean base, not copy, although I personally wouldn't mind copy). I really liked seeing the Architect in the Core, and her charms are definitely ones that could apply to Exigents of other city-gods, not just the Exigent of Wu-Jian's city god. I could easily have had the PCs meet the Exigent of some local City-God and just used some of her charms, plus maybe making up 1 or 2 to fit the theme of their own city.<br /> <br /> But saying &quot;Here is the Exigent of the Boar-God, and here is the Exigent of the Ape-God, just to show you how they're completely different and you definitely can't have your Exigent of the Bear-God have charms that are in any way similar&quot; is actually not much use in helping me make an Exigent of the Bear-God. Though showing me the Exigent of the Boar-God and the Exigent of the Bear-God, to give me both examples of charms that would be suitable for any animal-exigent (like, say &quot;Summon Boars/Apes&quot; or &quot;Command Boars/Apes&quot;) and charms that are more specific (tenacity of the boar, climbing of an ape) that would not be suitable, would be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-22-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T10:08:59-08:00","id":1020935,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;you're not allowed to have the same charms.&quot; Is a straw man that is not at all what Isator was saying, rather that if they have the same charms, it is not due to reasons of being in-universe of a &quot;shared category of Exigent&quot; because Exigents are unique. Rather, if they have the same charm, it's because you or the ST liked that Charm and chose to make it available to a different Exigent, and since Charms are not this in-universe construct anyway, it's not really a big deal at all.<br /> <br /> Constructing two Exigents of animal gods in totally different fashions helps to illustrate how unique they are, but nobody is going to tell you that you can't repurpose a charm from one for another.<br /> <br /> You'll run into potential issues of thematic or mechanical disconnect maybe if you don't tweak it a bit to suit the given Exigent, but that's not really like an Exigent problem, and it's really about if you're satisfied with it or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T12:03:02-08:00","id":1020964,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure, that's all fine. I don't really care about the semantics of whether Bear-God-Exigent and Boar-God-Exigent are the same &quot;class&quot; of Exigents or not. Like, I'm fine if all city-god-exigents are &quot;Architects&quot; as some particular metaphyiscal category, and I'm fine if that's just what the book calls them as a shorthand because it's easier, and I'm fine if there is a little sidebar telling you how important it is that every single Exigent is a special snowflake and not part of a broad category (beyond Exigent or Exalt).<br /> That all seems pretty unimportant to me.<br /> I just want stuff that I can take from one example and apply it to other things, and this is the easiest way.<br /> Homebrewing is hard work, frankly, for both player and ST. I'd like it kept as easy and simple as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-22-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T12:21:43-08:00","id":1020968,"title":"","content":"I don't mind, I guess, the term Architect as an out of universe, reader abstraction for Chosen of City Gods. I think I would be disappointed if it were a restrictive and in universe category (one among many), that implied a well defined and recognized in universe type of Exigent with specific restrictions they can't achieve, and well defined patterns of strengths and weaknesses, and a defined and fixed extent of overlaps with other Exalted. That really does seem to roll all over the &quot;Chosen of Whatever You Want&quot; attraction. The whole point seems that you don't, y'know, really have to accept some restriction in the books, or that if you do, the set of restrictions and definitions you have to accept is very minimal, and you can create a character as broad and powerful and flavored exactly as you wish, so long as you remain internally consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T12:23:25-08:00","id":1020969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1020555#post1020555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many Exigents are unique one-offs, in which case Castes/Aspects/etc. wouldn't make a sense at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it possible, in theory, to have a group of Exigents who share the same origination and, as such, could have Castes or such?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T12:52:57-08:00","id":1020980,"title":"","content":"Really, I would say the simplest reason to call the Chosen of several different city gods Architects is because the setting makes it feel unlikely that there would be more than one Chosen of a city god at the same time, at least within the scope of somebody's game.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's another thing that ought to be considered about them; the potential is broad, but the notion of the setting is that there are only about, what, a hundred going around in the Time of Tumult? Not really likely to be very much more of them in the works? There are a <i>lot</i> more things to be Chosen of than a hundred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T14:13:02-08:00","id":1021002,"title":"","content":"If you look closely at the blurb for Revana Quin it implies she might actually be the Exalted Of The God Of Cities In General. It would make sense that this god might have used the exigence multiple times on behalf of his various terrestrial-divinity subordinates.<br /> <br /> I expect we'll get Architects and maybe a few other &quot;exigent types&quot; written up as mini-splats in the exigents book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T14:41:52-08:00","id":1021017,"title":"","content":"What I'm expecting from this book is more of a Template that we can modify to suit the needs of the Exigent we seek to create.<br /> <br /> Just like how the spirit charms in previous editions were more or less classified in broad terms and categories, but given unique expression depending on the spirit that was using them, this is how I see Exigent charms being shown. While a Forest Spirit and a River Spirit could both have a version of the Hurry Home charm that allowed them to cross their domain almost instantly (don't have my books handy so I am not sure I am referring to the right charm), their expression of that charm would differ greatly. The River spirit may dissolve into the river it governs and reform anywhere along its length... while the Forest Spirit may enter one tree and exit another at the desired location. Mechanically, the two charms function the same, hence the reason they are both referred to by the same general charm name... but each is expressed in a unique way (and likely called different names by the spirit in question... provided the spirit even bothers to distinguish it as such).<br /> <br /> \u200bI see the Exigent book doing something fairly similar, providing charm templates that accomplish specific effects that can be modified (both thematically and even mechanically) to fit nearly any Exigent one could think of. One volcano Exigent may embody the destructive forces of his patron God, with a focus on combat and other destructive uses of Essence... while a different Exigent might focus on the creative and nurturing power of a different volcano god... and thus focus on craft and even medicinal type charms. By the same token, two different Exigents from two different gods could both be Architects in different way, yet have charms that do similar things... the only difference being more thematic than mechanical.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo be brutally honest, this is the only way I can honestly see a book on Exigents being even remotely viable. If the book more or less tells us to create whatever we want however we want to without at least some templates to help guide us... it may end up being another 1st Ed Lunar book... mechanically unworkable and a complete mess. Of course I do admit that my own bias may be influencing my opinion, and given the talent assembled on this project and I hopeful that I will be surprised by the end result, even if it is completely different from my expectations (very likely since this is a truly unique Exalt type).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:01:18-08:00","id":1021024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1021002#post1021002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look closely at the blurb for Revana Quin it implies she might actually be the Exalted Of The God Of Cities In General. It would make sense that this god might have used the exigence multiple times on behalf of his various terrestrial-divinity subordinates.<br /> <br /> I expect we'll get Architects and maybe a few other &quot;exigent types&quot; written up as mini-splats in the exigents book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revana and other Architects are the Chosen of Wun Ja, God of the Shining Metropolis (at least, as I conceived them). She's detailed in Second Edition\u2014I think the Compassbook for Yu-Shan? She went unmentioned because I wanted to avoid people confusing Wu-Jian/Wun Ja.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:02:54-08:00","id":1021027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1020969#post1020969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible, in theory, to have a group of Exigents who share the same origination</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though they're in the minority. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as such, could have Castes or such? </div> </div> </div>They could have Castespects, or they could not. It depends on what fits that type of Exigent and their divine patron best\u2014I wouldn't give them Castes unless I felt I had really good concepts for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:25:59-08:00","id":1021038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1021017#post1021017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm expecting from this book is more of a Template that we can modify to suit the needs of the Exigent we seek to create.<br /> <br /> Just like how the spirit charms in previous editions</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit Charms <i>now</i> aren't even designed like that, for reasons including that it was very dull, hard to effectively represent what the powers of distinct spirits were, and not really suited to representing nuances in their power.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bTo be brutally honest, this is the only way I can honestly see a book on Exigents being even remotely viable. If the book more or less tells us to create whatever we want however we want to without at least some templates to help guide us</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is a false dichotomy.<br /> <br /> The term &quot;Charm matrix&quot; has been floated around.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:38:30-08:00","id":1021046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1021027#post1021027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could have Castespects, or they could not. It depends on what fits that type of Exigent and their divine patron best\u2014I wouldn't give them Castes unless I felt I had really good concepts for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I was thinking of something like say, a Power Rangers-style sentai team, where spirit-Zordon imbues a group of cocky young teenagers with powers, but with each one having a slightly different focus in what they're good at, so that they can fight evil or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:37:15-08:00","id":1038585,"title":"","content":"I wanted to ask everyones opinion about something im about to do as an ST in one of my games. A number of forsaken gods (like Han Tha and others who do not fight with the Incarnae during the primordial war) have stolen a number of exigent exaltations and in order to wreak havoc on heaven have decided to infuse mortal champions with exaltations that fit their milieu. They plan to lead a rebellion against Yu-Shan by exalting a bunch of folks and then unleashing a number of demons on creation if possible. With heaven distracted with Yozi's they'll build while Yu-Shan and Malfeas fight and then step in towards the end while both sides are weak. Or at least thats how they'd plan it. Anyway exigents are making small moves in the tiny kingdom the PCs are going through and are generally causing problems. My question is, would it be ridiculous in 3e for those forsaken gods to steal exigent exaltations and use them in the manner i have contrived? Let me know your thoughts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8897-joshopotamus","name":"joshopotamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:47:17-08:00","id":1038591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>joshopotamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1038585#post1038585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is, would it be ridiculous in 3e for those forsaken gods to steal exigent exaltations and use them in the manner i have contrived?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNot at all. The idea that sometimes the Exigence gets illegally co-opted, often by gods who operate outside of the Celestial Order, to create unsanctioned Exalted was one of the first things we were told about the concept.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:58:40-08:00","id":1038767,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that many of the gods in question will be sacrificing themselves to do so. Their hate-on for Heaven had better be worth risking dying for.<br /> <br /> If memory serves, the Han-Tha we've seen is not the type to sacrifice a bunch of his power; is this nebulous revenge so great as to overshadow his desire to consume his way to the top?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-27-2017, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:52:40-08:00","id":1039060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1038591#post1038591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNot at all. The idea that sometimes the Exigence gets illegally co-opted, often by gods who operate outside of the Celestial Order, to create unsanctioned Exalted was one of the first things we were told about the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't they given a name? Black Market Exigence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T13:18:58-08:00","id":1039075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1039060#post1039060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weren't they given a name? Black Market Exigence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not convinced that's an official name, like a title, so much as a general description. But yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T18:35:26-08:00","id":1039190,"title":"","content":"i always saw it as han tha convincing others to do so. Or if he did he passed off the exigence and then spent time building up and passed it off again and rinse repeated. I'm thinking he might have gotten them during the great contagion and balorian crusade when i'd assume heaven was giving exigencies away like popcorn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8897-joshopotamus","name":"joshopotamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T18:52:53-08:00","id":1039198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes#post1020541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title pretty much says it but if they do/will/should what would they be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will the Exigents have castes? If a god makes multiple Exigents instead of just one, I suppose they could be divided into castes/aspects/classes etc. So, sure, why not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes#post1020541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally what powers do we think that all extigents should innately have?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've wondered the same thing. I've heard that their power level will range from dragonblooded to Solar, so I have no idea. Right now any exigence created Exalt the players come across in my game have the basic traits all Exalted share; fast healing, immunity to sickness, soaking lethal damage, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes#post1020541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And lastly what is the title for exigents? (Like Lawgiver or Stewards)</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is that since all the exigents are unique and as different as Abyssals to dragonblooded, there isn't one catch all title for them. In fact, IIRC, the term &quot;Exigent&quot; isn't one that exists in Creation. The Exalted that are created by way of the exigence are generally referred to as &quot;Exalted.&quot; That being the case, I suppose &quot;Exigent&quot; could be a catch all title if you wanted it to be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes#post1020541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been using Herald as their title, does that seem appropriate or have other people come up with other titles for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it works for you go for it. For me, the title &quot;Herald&quot; conjures an idea as to what the Exalt's duties/obligations/reasons for being are. In other words, for me, a title such as &quot;Herald&quot; would be too confining a title for all the exigence created Exalted. I would use &quot;Herald&quot; as a type of Exalt, like Solar or Lunar. Or perhaps more specific such as the name of an aspect or caste of exigent Exalt when there are multiple Exalts of one god. Hope that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":362,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","user":"Darkon","date":". 01-27-2017, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T19:01:30-08:00","id":1039207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>joshopotamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1039190#post1039190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i always saw it as han tha convincing others to do so. Or if he did he passed off the exigence and then spent time building up and passed it off again and rinse repeated. I'm thinking he might have gotten them during the great contagion and balorian crusade when i'd assume heaven was giving exigencies away like popcorn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, this is all IIRC, but the Unconquered Sun stopped giving out the Exigence when he turned his back on Creation. So for the last however many centuries there have been only a couple dozen exigence created Exalted reincarnating around Creation (what I wonder is, how many of these have the Immaculate Order tracked down and taken control of?). However, the UcS has since resumed bestowing the Exigence upon the return of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T20:57:28-08:00","id":1039244,"title":"","content":"I have several Exigents in a play-by-post that I'm running (the current arc is taking place in Great Forks) and I've pretty much settled on a model for typifying them: there are Solar Exalted, Lunar Exalted, etc. Swap the word Exalted with the word Exigent, and make the first word something to do with their empowering deity.<br /> <br /> For instance, <i>Shoreline's Harlequin</i>, Chosen of Miseng, God of the Rolling River, is a River Exigent. <i>Claret O'Saar</i>, Chosen of Nepele, Goddess of Wayward Breezes, is a Gust Exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T22:22:57-08:00","id":1039262,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Forbidden Gods, FrivYeti came up with an idea that I'm planning on stealing shamelessly when the Exigents book comes out, but it might be useful for you too, joshopotamus. <br /> <br /> One of the Forbidden Gods (and Han Tha would actually be a pretty good choice for this) has managed to get several portions of the Exigence and convinced a number of gods to create Exalted together with them. Each god spends a fair amount of power to flavor and charge the various Exigencies, and Han Tha has killed himself providing the final energies necessary to activate all of them. So, now you have a bunch of Exigents which all look different and have different powers, but they all have this deep need to be part of something bigger, almost a hunger for it. But that's it. There isn't any other real sign of Han Tha's influence.<br /> <br /> Until one of them murders another of this specific group of exigents and absorbs their powers. After that, you develop an increasingly strong need to absorb all the rest, as well as blackouts, voices in your head, and other scary urges. If some one managed to become the last of these Exigents, holding all the power, Han Tha awakens and takes over your body and soul, becoming an Exalted Spirit and attaining true excellence..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T00:12:06-08:00","id":1039293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1020541-do-will-should-exigents-have-castes?p=1039262#post1039262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Forbidden Gods, FrivYeti came up with an idea that I'm planning on stealing shamelessly when the Exigents book comes out, but it might be useful for you too, joshopotamus.<br /> <br /> One of the Forbidden Gods (and Han Tha would actually be a pretty good choice for this) has managed to get several portions of the Exigence and convinced a number of gods to create Exalted together with them. Each god spends a fair amount of power to flavor and charge the various Exigencies, and Han Tha has killed himself providing the final energies necessary to activate all of them. So, now you have a bunch of Exigents which all look different and have different powers, but they all have this deep need to be part of something bigger, almost a hunger for it. But that's it. There isn't any other real sign of Han Tha's influence.<br /> <br /> Until one of them murders another of this specific group of exigents and absorbs their powers. After that, you develop an increasingly strong need to absorb all the rest, as well as blackouts, voices in your head, and other scary urges. If some one managed to become the last of these Exigents, holding all the power, Han Tha awakens and takes over your body and soul, becoming an Exalted Spirit and attaining true excellence..</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, hey, I was kind of noodling something relating to cannibalism to enhance an Exalt.<br /> <br /> I have a concept for an Exigent of a Pottery god who emphasizes Pottery as Containers. Said god was once part of a group of pottery gods who all went rogue.<br /> <br /> To emphasize Pottery as Container, the Exigent keeps their enlightenment (for lack of a better word) in jars that theoretically could become vessels for that Exigence when the Exigent dies.<br /> <br /> I kind of imagine at some point, the Exigent also cannibalizes the powers of the rogue/Forbidden pottery gods, which could form a basis for other castes/aspects based on what they emphasized regarding pottery (Pottery as Art, probably a Forbidden God of Pottery that Consumes its contents, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/214-brontes","name":"Brontes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T00:22:43-08:00","id":1039296,"title":"","content":"I have two Exigents who share the same origination in my game (I'm working on writing up all the mechanics to make these playable as PCs too but that will take a while longer until it's done). Instead of going with the caste route, the story is that the god split his power in two. One Exigent got his &quot;dark&quot; side and the other got his &quot;light&quot; side. They are angel-themed too and have the power to &quot;give the gift of wings&quot;. Because the two sisters are bonded to each other both in blood and in exigence, they are drawn to one another in a love-hate relationship. The &quot;caste limitations&quot; is that the Charm set is divided into four categories based around the god's themes, where one of the categories is locked away from one aspect of the exigence. If one of them would give her wings to the other, that other would be complete and gain access to the full exigence. That's also how they pass the exigence along (giving their wings away and effectively become mortal). The exigence can be as two split parts, as one broken part with another &quot;lost&quot; part (i.e. one part of the exigence can be gone forever, leaving the other broken), or as one complete whole---the latter is the strongest version when it comes to excellencies, mote pools and Charm access. So not really castes, but kind of a workaround to having two characters with similar powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}